WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.340
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:05.610 --> 00:09.647
Don't you think it'd be amazing if we could do that as a whole class?

3
00:10.215 --> 00:11.883
To my beloved wife.

4
00:11.950 --> 00:15.854
My class has come together as one, working hard for the culture festival.

5
00:17.455 --> 00:21.159
Meanwhile, for the first time, I felt like a real teacher.

6
00:21.860 --> 00:25.163
After I confronted her, a student of mine stopped

7
00:25.230 --> 00:27.565
trying to quit school.

8
00:28.133 --> 00:31.302
I felt I was finally becoming a Great Teacher, when…

9
00:31.369 --> 00:32.437
Soma Sato!

10
00:32.504 --> 00:34.005
Is Soma Sato here?

11
00:34.072 --> 00:35.907
What's wrong, Vice Principal?

12
00:35.974 --> 00:37.308
The police are here!

13
00:37.375 --> 00:38.943
To arrest him, they say!

14
00:39.511 --> 00:40.678
What?

15
00:46.551 --> 00:50.421
According to them, Soma Sato transported marijuana for a smuggling gang.

16
00:50.488 --> 00:53.258
They were raided, and they ratted him out.

17
00:54.092 --> 00:55.627
What is he doing, that idiot?

18
00:55.693 --> 00:58.730
Principal, this is the biggest scandal since our school's founding.

19
00:58.796 --> 01:02.133
I believe we have no choice but to expel him right away.

20
01:02.200 --> 01:03.468
I suppose so.

21
01:03.535 --> 01:05.069
Hold on a second!

22
01:05.136 --> 01:08.039
Can't we at least hear Soma's side of the story first?

23
01:08.706 --> 01:11.109
SHIN YOKOHAMA POLICE STATION

24
01:11.676 --> 01:16.814
This is the current situation, so can we hold off on the divorce

25
01:17.382 --> 01:19.584
until this is resolved?

26
01:41.706 --> 01:44.509
Do you live here alone?

27
01:44.576 --> 01:45.743
My parents

28
01:46.811 --> 01:49.514
wanted to get rid of me after I got held back a year.

29
01:52.951 --> 01:56.421
They said they'd rent an apartment for me. After that, I was on my own.

30
01:59.390 --> 02:00.725
Hey, Soma…

31
02:01.426 --> 02:03.828
Did you really transport marijuana?

32
02:08.032 --> 02:11.102
I'm sure they forced you into it, am I right?

33
02:11.869 --> 02:15.173
Those old classmates of yours who often came to our school.

34
02:16.107 --> 02:18.109
Why didn't you refuse?

35
02:18.776 --> 02:20.044
I did refuse.

36
02:21.212 --> 02:22.080
But?

37
02:24.882 --> 02:28.653
They said they'd hurt my classmates.

38
02:34.058 --> 02:38.296
Soma was just being threatened by his old delinquent friends,

39
02:38.363 --> 02:41.266
so please, be lenient with him!

40
02:41.933 --> 02:43.935
What do we do, Principal?

41
02:44.002 --> 02:45.069
Well,

42
02:45.903 --> 02:48.373
I consulted with our parent company,

43
02:48.940 --> 02:51.576
but it is a fact that he engaged in criminal activity,

44
02:52.644 --> 02:55.013
so I don't think we can avoid expelling him.

45
02:55.647 --> 02:57.482
I knew it.

46
02:57.548 --> 02:58.983
Hold on a second!

47
02:59.050 --> 03:00.585
If he doesn't like that,

48
03:00.652 --> 03:03.788
he can voluntarily drop out before the decision is made.

49
03:04.355 --> 03:06.324
Otherwise, he won't be able to go to any other school.

50
03:06.391 --> 03:08.293
-What? -What do you mean?

51
03:08.359 --> 03:10.161
You're a teacher, and you don't know?

52
03:10.728 --> 03:13.765
A student who gets expelled can't transfer anywhere.

53
03:17.835 --> 03:18.670
Damn it.

54
03:19.237 --> 03:22.240
That Nakamaru bastard was as good as threatening us.

55
03:22.307 --> 03:24.509
PRINCIPAL'S OFFICE

56
03:24.575 --> 03:26.044
CLASS 1-B

57
03:26.110 --> 03:28.746
Anyone with a question, please raise your hand!

58
03:28.813 --> 03:31.716
Are you all good? Is there anything you don't understand?

59
03:31.783 --> 03:32.984
Don't worry.

60
03:33.685 --> 03:37.155
You just need to keep studying with everyone as usual.

61
03:38.356 --> 03:39.424
I'm dropping out.

62
03:39.490 --> 03:41.359
What are you talking about?

63
03:41.426 --> 03:44.762
I can't cause any more trouble for you or the class.

64
03:46.764 --> 03:48.132
Oh, all right.

65
03:50.635 --> 03:54.672
Then, before you do, shall we go there together?

66
03:55.873 --> 03:56.774
Huh?

67
04:10.421 --> 04:11.823
So it's you punks?

68
04:12.590 --> 04:17.295
Are you the ones trying to ruin my precious student's youth?

69
04:17.929 --> 04:20.398
Huh? What if we are?

70
04:23.835 --> 04:28.039
Could you stay away from Soma?

71
04:30.475 --> 04:35.680
Sure, he used to hang out with you and got held back a grade.

72
04:36.314 --> 04:38.516
But he worked hard to graduate middle school,

73
04:39.217 --> 04:43.788
and right now, he's trying to enjoy the wonders of youth.

74
04:44.589 --> 04:47.425
So, could you just leave him alone?

75
04:51.629 --> 04:52.697
I'm begging you!

76
04:55.199 --> 04:56.467
Like I give a damn!

77
04:57.201 --> 05:00.405
You're pathetic too, crying to your homeroom teacher.

78
05:00.972 --> 05:03.474
Or are you looking down on us

79
05:03.541 --> 05:05.643
because only you got to attend high school?

80
05:05.710 --> 05:06.878
What "youth"?

81
05:07.445 --> 05:10.615
Trash like you doesn't deserve anything like that!

82
05:11.182 --> 05:12.383
You bastards!

83
05:15.887 --> 05:19.457
If you do that, you'll really get expelled.

84
05:19.524 --> 05:20.491
I don't care!

85
05:20.558 --> 05:21.492
You idiot!

86
05:21.559 --> 05:23.194
I told you to be smart.

87
05:24.228 --> 05:28.966
Right now, what's right in front of you is what you'd call "the line."

88
05:29.934 --> 05:31.969
Whatever you do, don't ever cross that line.

89
05:34.305 --> 05:36.741
I just said something really cool.

90
05:38.176 --> 05:40.178
What kind of nonsense are you spouting?

91
05:40.244 --> 05:42.146
-You're weird, old man! -Shut up!

92
05:42.814 --> 05:44.449
My beloved wife

93
05:44.515 --> 05:49.520
just told me to sign divorce papers, so I'm super pissed off right now!

94
05:49.587 --> 05:50.988
Who gives a shit!

95
05:53.658 --> 05:54.826
You bastard!

96
06:00.398 --> 06:01.399
Come on!

97
06:04.335 --> 06:05.169
Hey!

98
06:13.611 --> 06:14.445
What?

99
06:15.079 --> 06:16.280
Come at me barehanded.

100
06:19.417 --> 06:20.418
Don't get involved!

101
06:20.485 --> 06:21.652
Go!

102
06:22.887 --> 06:24.088
It hurts!

103
06:24.155 --> 06:25.490
Let go! That hurts!

104
06:25.556 --> 06:27.058
-You old man! -Let go!

105
06:27.692 --> 06:28.359
Let go!

106
06:29.227 --> 06:31.295
-What? -Get ready, it's going to sting.

107
06:32.430 --> 06:34.432
It hurts! Hey!

108
06:35.266 --> 06:37.535
Hey, be gentler.

109
06:38.135 --> 06:41.506
This is what you get for being so reckless at your age.

110
06:42.240 --> 06:46.177
When I was young, guys like that were nothing to me.

111
06:46.244 --> 06:47.311
I'm going to

112
06:48.446 --> 06:50.181
drop out of school.

113
06:50.248 --> 06:50.982
What?

114
06:51.549 --> 06:52.817
Just like they said,

115
06:53.417 --> 06:55.620
someone like me has no right to enjoy their youth.

116
06:55.686 --> 06:57.488
Stop talking nonsense.

117
06:58.055 --> 07:00.858
No matter what happens, stay in school.

118
07:00.925 --> 07:03.294
Participate in the culture festival with the whole class.

119
07:03.861 --> 07:04.762
But…

120
07:04.829 --> 07:08.566
Don't worry. I'll figure the rest out somehow.

121
07:09.567 --> 07:10.434
Okay.

122
07:11.435 --> 07:13.604
-I'm heading off then, Murai. -Right.

123
07:13.671 --> 07:14.505
Bye.

124
07:14.572 --> 07:16.474
Yeah. Take care of yourself.

125
07:18.609 --> 07:20.344
What on earth is he planning to do?

126
07:20.411 --> 07:21.579
Who knows?

127
07:21.646 --> 07:25.416
Onicchi has always been unpredictable.

128
07:25.483 --> 07:26.517
Is that so?

129
07:27.084 --> 07:30.621
Back when I was a student too, he risked his life trying to protect me.

130
07:30.688 --> 07:32.189
Murai! Hurry up and run!

131
07:33.591 --> 07:37.395
Why does he always do such reckless things?

132
07:38.296 --> 07:39.697
He probably just…

133
07:41.365 --> 07:44.168
doesn't want to leave us all alone out here.

134
07:44.902 --> 07:45.736
What?

135
07:46.704 --> 07:49.974
Going to high school, making friends,

136
07:50.808 --> 07:52.810
and creating tons of memories…

137
07:53.477 --> 07:56.047
How important that is for us…

138
07:57.548 --> 08:00.551
Onicchi knows better than anyone else.

139
08:07.959 --> 08:09.460
What's this?

140
08:09.527 --> 08:13.130
A TEACHER OF SEISHIN ACADEMY ASSAULTED PEOPLE

141
08:13.197 --> 08:15.633
DIDN'T HE USE TO BE A BIKE GANG MEMBER TOO?

142
08:15.700 --> 08:16.834
Hey, come on.

143
08:16.901 --> 08:20.004
It's already been shared a whole bunch.

144
08:24.408 --> 08:25.409
Onizuka!

145
08:28.012 --> 08:29.847
What on earth were you thinking?

146
08:29.914 --> 08:31.849
A teacher, committing assault?

147
08:32.617 --> 08:35.353
Those kids' families are making a huge fuss, saying they'll sue!

148
08:35.419 --> 08:36.587
I'm sorry.

149
08:36.654 --> 08:40.424
They were threatening Soma, but they played dumb, which pissed me off.

150
08:40.491 --> 08:42.093
How can you be so nonchalant?

151
08:42.727 --> 08:44.829
Parents are flooding us with inquiries!

152
08:44.895 --> 08:47.264
They're asking why we let such a violent teacher run free!

153
08:47.331 --> 08:50.067
It'll be fine. Just explain what happened, properly…

154
08:50.134 --> 08:52.303
It's obvious that won't work!

155
08:52.370 --> 08:54.205
As things stand, you…

156
08:55.506 --> 08:57.942
will have to leave this school along with Soma Sato!

157
08:58.009 --> 08:59.910
Hold on a second.

158
08:59.977 --> 09:02.413
Soma was being threatened,

159
09:02.480 --> 09:05.483
and he told me right away about him delivering the marijuana.

160
09:05.549 --> 09:06.617
What?

161
09:07.618 --> 09:09.420
What do you mean by that?

162
09:09.487 --> 09:10.321
You…

163
09:10.388 --> 09:15.026
You knew a student committed a crime and didn't report it?

164
09:15.593 --> 09:16.360
Yes.

165
09:16.427 --> 09:17.928
"Yes" isn't the answer.

166
09:19.030 --> 09:21.832
That's a cover-up!

167
09:21.899 --> 09:23.501
Soma did nothing wrong,

168
09:23.567 --> 09:26.871
so I thought if I made them admit to the crime, it would be all good.

169
09:26.937 --> 09:30.441
This time you are getting fired for sure!

170
09:30.508 --> 09:31.909
Submit your resignation now!

171
09:31.976 --> 09:33.544
Then, how about this?

172
09:33.611 --> 09:35.279
Forget about me for a bit,

173
09:35.346 --> 09:37.915
and just give Soma a one-week suspension, okay?

174
09:37.982 --> 09:40.651
What are you talking about? If we don't expel him,

175
09:40.718 --> 09:44.155
it will set a bad precedent, so we have no choice but to be strict!

176
09:44.221 --> 09:45.256
Wait a minute!

177
09:45.322 --> 09:47.458
You accept this decision, right, Principal?

178
09:47.525 --> 09:49.060
Well…

179
09:49.927 --> 09:51.395
I suppose so.

180
09:53.431 --> 09:57.435
Mr. Onizuka, it is very unfortunate,

181
09:58.235 --> 09:59.837
but Soma Sato must be…

182
10:02.573 --> 10:04.408
Excuse me for the interruption.

183
10:04.475 --> 10:06.177
What brings you here, Director Katayama?

184
10:06.811 --> 10:10.848
I came to apologize for the trouble caused by Ryunosuke Miyazawa,

185
10:10.915 --> 10:13.084
the employee our company dispatched.

186
10:13.150 --> 10:16.153
You didn't need to come all the way here just for that…

187
10:16.220 --> 10:20.458
And, the student who was arrested by the police,

188
10:21.258 --> 10:23.360
we would like an update on him.

189
10:24.428 --> 10:27.164
I see, so that's how it is.

190
10:29.567 --> 10:30.701
Mr. Onizuka.

191
10:32.069 --> 10:32.970
Yes.

192
10:33.771 --> 10:37.508
Regrettably, we have no choice but to ask you to resign.

193
10:38.409 --> 10:40.544
You're amazing, Director Katayama.

194
10:41.112 --> 10:44.582
You truly understand. Well then, Soma Sato will also…

195
10:44.648 --> 10:46.951
A strict warning should be enough for him.

196
10:47.918 --> 10:50.154
After all, the ones at fault were those youths

197
10:50.721 --> 10:54.792
and his teacher, who knew his student was involved in a crime

198
10:55.359 --> 10:59.430
yet covered it up and committed violence.

199
10:59.497 --> 11:00.831
Mr. Onizuka.

200
11:00.898 --> 11:02.500
No, but…

201
11:12.877 --> 11:15.746
Are you really okay with this?

202
11:17.848 --> 11:18.949
Thank you very much.

203
11:19.517 --> 11:20.484
But…

204
11:21.152 --> 11:24.455
If you quit, Kenta will be sad.

205
11:25.356 --> 11:27.992
Thanks to you, he actually felt like going to school

206
11:28.659 --> 11:30.327
and has been having fun every day.

207
11:31.762 --> 11:34.365
He'll be fine now.

208
11:35.666 --> 11:36.901
He's not alone anymore.

209
11:38.369 --> 11:39.370
I see.

210
11:46.177 --> 11:47.978
So that's how it is.

211
11:49.180 --> 11:53.050
You're taking all the blame to save Soma, aren't you?

212
11:55.152 --> 11:57.121
I mean, come on.

213
11:57.855 --> 12:01.425
I can't let my dear student get a stain on his record

214
12:02.026 --> 12:03.961
over something as stupid as this.

215
12:04.695 --> 12:05.663
Could it be

216
12:06.330 --> 12:09.200
that it was also you who posted all of this, Mr. Onizuka?

217
12:09.266 --> 12:11.302
A TEACHER OF SEISHIN ACADEMY ASSAULTED PEOPLE

218
12:11.368 --> 12:13.103
DIDN'T HE USE TO BE A BIKE GANG MEMBER TOO?

219
12:18.142 --> 12:19.710
This is terrible.

220
12:20.211 --> 12:22.646
So Onicchi is taking the fall for Soma?

221
12:23.414 --> 12:24.882
No way!

222
12:24.949 --> 12:25.983
What should we do?

223
12:31.121 --> 12:31.989
Soma!

224
12:37.761 --> 12:39.663
Hey, what do you think you're doing?

225
12:39.730 --> 12:41.665
Isn't it obvious? I'm telling the truth.

226
12:41.732 --> 12:42.766
You idiot.

227
12:43.734 --> 12:47.838
I used up all of my meager intelligence to come up with this plan,

228
12:47.905 --> 12:49.039
so don't ruin it.

229
12:49.106 --> 12:51.008
Why did you lie?

230
12:51.075 --> 12:54.178
You didn't know I transported marijuana!

231
13:08.125 --> 13:09.894
When I was younger,

232
13:11.595 --> 13:13.230
I used to strut around

233
13:14.064 --> 13:16.533
with my hands shoved in my pockets just like you.

234
13:18.068 --> 13:19.570
Until a certain person told me…

235
13:21.639 --> 13:22.940
"Mr. Onizuka,

236
13:24.241 --> 13:28.879
hands aren't meant for doing that.

237
13:31.715 --> 13:34.318
They're meant for holding onto precious things.

238
13:36.553 --> 13:40.925
For connecting with people you care about."

239
13:43.427 --> 13:45.562
Didn't she teach you that?

240
13:46.297 --> 13:48.232
After all, she was your grandma.

241
13:50.267 --> 13:51.101
What?

242
14:11.422 --> 14:14.758
The reason I was able to become a teacher…

243
14:15.960 --> 14:17.795
was all thanks to your grandma.

244
14:19.229 --> 14:21.031
If I hadn't met the Chairperson,

245
14:21.098 --> 14:25.102
I'd still be a hopeless piece of trash.

246
14:29.006 --> 14:30.007
Hey, Soma.

247
14:31.342 --> 14:34.979
If you get expelled like this, your grandma will be heartbroken.

248
14:36.647 --> 14:37.614
No,

249
14:38.482 --> 14:40.050
she'd definitely be angry.

250
14:41.885 --> 14:46.523
"This happened because you were building a shell around yourself.

251
14:47.624 --> 14:53.163
Stop acting foolish, tell your classmates and teachers

252
14:53.931 --> 14:56.000
how you actually feel."

253
14:56.967 --> 14:58.502
That is what she'd say.

254
15:06.243 --> 15:09.079
SEISHIN HIGH SCHOOL PRINCIPAL YASUHIRO OHKUBO

255
15:09.146 --> 15:10.247
PRINCIPAL YASUHIRO OHKUBO

256
15:10.314 --> 15:13.951
Seems Mr. Onizuka's dismissal has been officially decided.

257
15:14.018 --> 15:16.487
But isn't there anything we can do?

258
15:17.654 --> 15:19.790
Ms. Kashiwabara, something has happened.

259
15:19.857 --> 15:20.824
Your class is…

260
15:21.692 --> 15:22.526
What?

261
15:28.399 --> 15:30.768
WE HEREBY BOYCOTT THE FESTIVAL AND WILL HOLE UP IN THE CLASSROOM

262
15:31.335 --> 15:33.070
Hey, everyone, what are you doing?

263
15:33.637 --> 15:34.705
Open up!

264
15:34.772 --> 15:39.376
We're not coming out of here until Mr. Onizuka comes back to school!

265
15:39.443 --> 15:42.379
I understand how you feel, but what good will doing this do?

266
15:42.446 --> 15:46.517
No matter what you say, we won't leave until our demand is met!

267
15:46.583 --> 15:47.618
Boycott!

268
15:47.684 --> 15:50.687
Boycott!

269
15:50.754 --> 15:53.157
Boycott!

270
15:54.258 --> 15:55.292
Really?

271
15:55.359 --> 15:56.460
What should we do?

272
15:57.061 --> 15:59.196
At this rate, things will get out of hand.

273
16:00.731 --> 16:01.899
Well…

274
16:03.500 --> 16:07.404
Until my punishment is handed down, I can't go to school.

275
16:08.272 --> 16:10.741
So there's nothing I can do.

276
16:11.341 --> 16:13.477
Why are you saying something so cold?

277
16:13.544 --> 16:16.547
Does Class 1-B not matter to you anymore?

278
16:19.550 --> 16:21.051
I'm so hungry!

279
16:21.118 --> 16:23.053
Hey, what about the bathroom?

280
16:23.120 --> 16:25.222
-Just hold it in. -I'm going to piss myself!

281
16:25.289 --> 16:27.124
Geez, aren't you the Big Bro?

282
16:27.191 --> 16:29.293
When is Onicchi getting here?

283
16:29.359 --> 16:30.394
Onicchi!

284
16:38.602 --> 16:39.870
Who could that be?

285
16:39.937 --> 16:41.972
Maybe Onicchi came for us?

286
16:42.039 --> 16:43.040
Onicchi?

287
16:43.107 --> 16:44.174
No way!

288
16:44.241 --> 16:46.844
Hey, Kotone! You're in there, right? Open up!

289
16:47.511 --> 16:49.513
No way! Dad?

290
16:49.580 --> 16:50.981
-What? -What?

291
16:56.186 --> 16:58.155
-Yo! -What are you doing?

292
16:58.222 --> 17:00.491
-Telling us to come out? -No, it's not like that.

293
17:01.058 --> 17:01.825
Then what?

294
17:01.892 --> 17:03.994
We did a barricade protest back then too, right?

295
17:04.061 --> 17:05.929
Yeah, we did!

296
17:05.996 --> 17:08.031
We were in Onicchi's class too, you see.

297
17:08.098 --> 17:10.834
Can we come in? We'll leave as soon as we're done.

298
17:10.901 --> 17:12.102
Oh, go ahead.

299
17:17.474 --> 17:20.644
This vibe really brings back memories.

300
17:20.711 --> 17:23.313
-Feels like we're going back to our youth. -Right?

301
17:23.380 --> 17:25.449
Excuse me. What did you come here for?

302
17:26.183 --> 17:28.819
Oh, sorry! We got a bit excited.

303
17:31.021 --> 17:36.660
We came to deliver a message from Mr. Onizuka, so to speak.

304
17:36.727 --> 17:40.330
That guy hasn't changed one bit. We're busy too, you know!

305
17:40.397 --> 17:42.866
He always made us run errands out of nowhere.

306
17:42.933 --> 17:45.435
Hey, speaking of which, Noboru do you remember?

307
17:45.502 --> 17:49.072
To see if bullying was fun, Onizuka hung you upside down from the roof!

308
17:50.040 --> 17:51.341
That was insane!

309
17:51.408 --> 17:52.376
-Right. -Yeah.

310
17:54.211 --> 17:56.813
-He really was out of control. -Seriously!

311
17:58.415 --> 17:59.616
But, you know,

312
18:00.918 --> 18:02.786
as you all probably know,

313
18:04.121 --> 18:07.925
being with him is really fun.

314
18:08.725 --> 18:09.626
He makes you feel

315
18:09.693 --> 18:12.996
like the world is only going to get better from here on out.

316
18:15.632 --> 18:16.833
Besides,

317
18:17.601 --> 18:20.037
when you get to our age, you realize…

318
18:20.604 --> 18:22.072
That in high school,

319
18:23.240 --> 18:27.377
you can make tons of memories that become treasures for a lifetime.

320
18:27.444 --> 18:29.479
GIVE ONICCHI BACK TO US!

321
18:29.546 --> 18:30.981
Knowing that,

322
18:32.349 --> 18:34.751
should you really be doing this?

323
18:34.818 --> 18:38.222
At the very least, Onicchi wouldn't be happy about it.

324
18:40.057 --> 18:43.994
"Your youth is precious, don't waste it!"

325
18:44.561 --> 18:45.896
That's what he'd say.

326
18:51.068 --> 18:54.605
Well, that's all from us.

327
18:54.671 --> 18:56.673
Let's get going. Sorry for intruding.

328
19:05.148 --> 19:07.417
Let's go for a drink at Murai's!

329
19:11.288 --> 19:12.389
Hey, everyone.

330
19:13.123 --> 19:14.858
Shall we practice for the festival?

331
19:14.925 --> 19:15.993
Yes.

332
19:16.059 --> 19:16.927
Let's do it.

333
19:16.994 --> 19:20.664
I'll go tell the teachers that we're stopping the barricade.

334
19:20.731 --> 19:24.935
Guys, let's take down the barricades so we can make space.

335
19:25.002 --> 19:27.638
Us girls will go buy drinks from the vending machine.

336
19:27.704 --> 19:29.106
Can I go to the toilet?

337
19:32.276 --> 19:34.778
All right, we'll start practice in ten minutes.

338
19:34.845 --> 19:36.580
-Okay! -Yes!

339
19:37.147 --> 19:37.814
Ken-Ken.

340
19:40.984 --> 19:43.787
Don't you think we could arrange and use this part?

341
19:43.854 --> 19:45.555
Oh, that's great!

342
19:52.796 --> 19:53.797
Hey, Yuukichi.

343
19:53.864 --> 19:55.032
What?

344
19:56.500 --> 19:58.402
Should we start dating?

345
19:58.468 --> 19:59.303
What?

346
20:00.570 --> 20:02.439
Don't say that. That's gross.

347
20:03.607 --> 20:05.309
You didn't have to be that harsh.

348
20:06.510 --> 20:08.879
I mean, we need to focus on practice right now.

349
20:08.945 --> 20:10.480
I know, but still.

350
20:11.014 --> 20:13.583
What are you two doing over there? We're practicing!

351
20:14.151 --> 20:17.654
All right, everyone, today we'll start from here.

352
20:18.355 --> 20:19.656
Everyone, take a seat.

353
20:19.723 --> 20:20.757
Sit down.

354
20:20.824 --> 20:22.292
Hurry up and sit down!

355
20:23.293 --> 20:26.830
At the zombie part, everyone always speeds up the tempo, so…

356
20:48.085 --> 20:49.586
Don't slack off, Soma.

357
20:50.587 --> 20:53.090
-What? -Come on, let's practice.

358
20:53.790 --> 20:55.726
-Let's go. -Come on, Soma.

359
20:55.792 --> 20:57.728
You're the worst at it.

360
20:57.794 --> 20:59.196
I'll teach you.

361
20:59.796 --> 21:01.231
I'm the second worst!

362
21:01.298 --> 21:02.332
What the heck?

363
21:06.002 --> 21:07.003
You guys…

364
21:09.306 --> 21:10.474
Why aren't you blaming me?

365
21:11.775 --> 21:15.178
Because of me, Mr. Onizuka got fired.

366
21:15.746 --> 21:17.147
It's not your fault.

367
21:18.248 --> 21:19.649
Besides,

368
21:20.317 --> 21:21.218
we're homeskillets.

369
21:21.952 --> 21:22.786
What?

370
21:22.853 --> 21:25.055
We're friends, aren't we?

371
21:27.724 --> 21:28.558
Lately,

372
21:30.427 --> 21:32.229
that song,

373
21:33.163 --> 21:36.199
"When I Become a First Grader" has been stuck in my head.

374
21:39.236 --> 21:41.538
You were calling each other by nicknames,

375
21:42.606 --> 21:46.810
and I felt so miserable being the only one left out.

376
21:50.313 --> 21:54.084
When I become a first-grader

377
21:54.151 --> 21:58.088
When I become a first-grader

378
21:58.655 --> 22:02.692
I wonder if I can make 100 friends?

379
22:02.759 --> 22:06.563
I want to eat with 100 people

380
22:06.630 --> 22:10.400
Eating rice balls on top of Mount Fuji

381
22:10.967 --> 22:14.871
Chomp, chomp

382
22:14.938 --> 22:18.442
When I become a first-grader

383
22:18.508 --> 22:22.379
When I become a first-grader

384
22:22.446 --> 22:26.116
I wonder if I can make 100 friends?

385
22:26.683 --> 22:29.920
I want to laugh with 100 people

386
22:30.487 --> 22:33.757
Making the whole world shake

387
22:40.764 --> 22:44.468
From now on, let's do lots of things together, all 28 of us.

388
22:45.936 --> 22:46.870
Soma.

389
22:48.271 --> 22:49.272
Thank you.

390
22:53.410 --> 22:55.278
I'm really glad I ended up

391
22:57.481 --> 22:58.782
in this class.

392
23:04.087 --> 23:06.022
SEISHIN FESTIVAL

393
23:06.690 --> 23:08.959
An announcement for all students.

394
23:09.025 --> 23:11.962
The festival starts in an hour.

395
23:12.462 --> 23:16.032
Each class, please proceed with the final checks.

396
23:26.943 --> 23:29.646
Are you really fine with this?

397
23:31.448 --> 23:32.682
How about you?

398
23:33.250 --> 23:35.418
How have things been at your company?

399
23:36.720 --> 23:37.888
I've decided to quit.

400
23:39.856 --> 23:42.158
Oh? Then, what are you going to do now?

401
23:43.493 --> 23:46.263
I'm thinking of taking the teacher employment exam.

402
23:47.163 --> 23:48.131
Seriously?

403
23:56.373 --> 23:58.275
You'd better not.

404
23:59.709 --> 24:04.114
Once you're a teacher, your skills aren't transferable,

405
24:04.180 --> 24:05.749
and you can't change careers.

406
24:05.815 --> 24:08.652
You never know where parents might be watching,

407
24:08.718 --> 24:12.355
so even when you go out drinking, you have to go far from the school.

408
24:13.590 --> 24:17.127
Still, there's no job as wonderful as this, is there?

409
24:19.062 --> 24:23.900
After all, you get to nurture unique individuals.

410
24:27.971 --> 24:30.040
I suppose so.

411
24:31.608 --> 24:32.742
STAFF ROOM

412
24:32.809 --> 24:33.944
Everyone.

413
24:34.511 --> 24:37.514
It was only for a short while, but thanks for everything.

414
24:40.317 --> 24:41.418
It's such a shame.

415
24:42.352 --> 24:45.221
I wanted to see what you'd teach our students

416
24:45.789 --> 24:46.957
just a little more.

417
24:47.624 --> 24:48.558
Me too.

418
24:48.625 --> 24:53.663
Thanks to you, teaching has finally become fun for me.

419
24:53.730 --> 24:55.832
I wouldn't go that far,

420
24:56.666 --> 24:59.736
but, I guess I wanted to talk with you more.

421
25:00.770 --> 25:01.638
Everyone,

422
25:03.073 --> 25:04.107
take care.

423
25:06.242 --> 25:07.677
Principal, Vice Principal!

424
25:08.445 --> 25:09.412
What is it?

425
25:09.479 --> 25:14.050
Could you let Mr. Onizuka teach one last lesson?

426
25:15.352 --> 25:19.055
I think the students of Class 1-B would want to say a proper goodbye too.

427
25:19.856 --> 25:21.024
Please!

428
25:21.091 --> 25:23.460
Obviously we won't allow that!

429
25:23.526 --> 25:25.362
-But-- -I said no!

430
25:25.428 --> 25:26.496
It's fine.

431
25:26.563 --> 25:27.964
What? What are you saying?

432
25:28.031 --> 25:29.699
I am the Principal.

433
25:30.233 --> 25:31.534
I am the one who decides.

434
25:31.601 --> 25:32.669
No, but--

435
25:32.736 --> 25:33.837
Just…

436
25:35.105 --> 25:36.740
Shut up for a bit!

437
25:37.240 --> 25:41.611
Every single time I try to say something, you always jump in and speak first!

438
25:42.245 --> 25:45.582
I'll admit, I speak rather slowly.

439
25:45.649 --> 25:49.519
Besides, because I'm the only one here without a teaching license,

440
25:49.586 --> 25:52.689
I had an odd complex toward all of you.

441
25:54.290 --> 25:55.392
But,

442
25:56.993 --> 26:00.063
watching Mr. Onizuka made me reflect on myself.

443
26:02.332 --> 26:06.970
No matter your position, you have to believe in yourself more!

444
26:09.105 --> 26:12.342
Therefore, as Principal,

445
26:12.409 --> 26:14.844
I am going to reform this school from here on out.

446
26:15.412 --> 26:17.147
As I don't have a teaching license,

447
26:17.213 --> 26:20.083
I can come up with ideas that none of you would think of.

448
26:20.650 --> 26:22.452
For example, at a school overseas,

449
26:22.519 --> 26:28.224
I hear their harshest punishment is making the student punch the principal.

450
26:28.992 --> 26:32.195
To teach them that punching someone hurts themselves as well…

451
26:32.262 --> 26:34.064
I was thinking, we could do that.

452
26:35.065 --> 26:39.769
Look, the way my body is built, if I get hit a bit…

453
26:40.837 --> 26:44.074
See?

454
26:48.945 --> 26:52.082
Did I just make it weird?

455
27:03.593 --> 27:05.195
Thank you for everything.

456
27:05.261 --> 27:08.064
Meeting all of you was really fun.

457
27:09.833 --> 27:10.900
Is that all?

458
27:11.835 --> 27:12.702
Is that not okay?

459
27:12.769 --> 27:16.439
You aren't a student transferring out! Say something more befitting a teacher!

460
27:16.506 --> 27:19.342
I've never been in this situation before.

461
27:19.409 --> 27:21.411
I'm kind of nervous.

462
27:26.382 --> 27:30.520
I mean, well, you know…

463
27:34.157 --> 27:37.060
Ms. Kashiwabara, please say something like you always do.

464
27:37.127 --> 27:39.796
Give me a break. I'm not the one quitting.

465
27:39.863 --> 27:41.364
Hold on a second.

466
27:42.065 --> 27:42.899
Hey.

467
27:49.405 --> 27:51.674
Well, you know.

468
27:53.376 --> 27:54.778
I mean…

469
27:56.613 --> 27:57.781
Mr. Onizuka!

470
28:10.460 --> 28:11.427
Ken-Ken.

471
28:11.995 --> 28:15.698
Thanks to you coming back to school,

472
28:15.765 --> 28:18.668
I was able to remain the homeroom teacher of Class 1-B.

473
28:19.702 --> 28:20.937
You're the kind of person who,

474
28:21.604 --> 28:25.108
if I mess up, would pat me on the back and say things will be okay.

475
28:26.376 --> 28:27.644
That is your strength.

476
28:28.311 --> 28:30.947
So don't ever forget that.

477
28:32.382 --> 28:34.450
Copy that, Mr. Onizuka.

478
28:39.489 --> 28:40.690
Yuukichi,

479
28:41.891 --> 28:44.561
thanks to you saying you wanted to start a Drill Team,

480
28:45.695 --> 28:47.964
the class was able to come together as one.

481
28:48.865 --> 28:49.899
Thank you.

482
28:51.067 --> 28:54.070
Your name means "bonds,"

483
28:54.137 --> 28:57.273
and you have the strength to bind people together.

484
28:58.007 --> 29:02.378
Don't ever lose your courage, and keep on connecting people together.

485
29:04.247 --> 29:06.916
Leave it to me, Mr. Onizuka.

486
29:10.720 --> 29:11.888
Momocchi.

487
29:12.989 --> 29:14.123
Keep slaying.

488
29:15.091 --> 29:15.925
What?

489
29:16.559 --> 29:17.660
What do you mean?

490
29:18.294 --> 29:19.295
Work hard and stay healthy.

491
29:19.863 --> 29:21.731
What? That's all you have to say?

492
29:21.798 --> 29:25.134
You know, the day you and the others sang me "Happy Birthday"

493
29:25.201 --> 29:27.503
was the best birthday of my life!

494
29:28.471 --> 29:30.006
Don't say that.

495
29:30.540 --> 29:33.376
Make next year and the next great birthdays too!

496
29:34.577 --> 29:37.947
You always work hard to brighten up those around you.

497
29:39.048 --> 29:40.350
You can do it.

498
29:41.851 --> 29:43.853
Okay, Mr. Onizuka.

499
29:49.125 --> 29:50.093
Big Bro.

500
29:52.262 --> 29:53.129
I'm sorry.

501
29:53.730 --> 29:55.665
Huh? For what?

502
29:57.333 --> 30:01.170
When I heard you say you didn't want to punch anyone anymore,

503
30:02.138 --> 30:04.140
I swore I'd do the same,

504
30:04.841 --> 30:07.277
but in the end, I broke that oath.

505
30:08.244 --> 30:11.781
Still, you have to keep that promise.

506
30:11.848 --> 30:14.784
Because of kind, hard-working people like you,

507
30:15.351 --> 30:17.687
this world can still go on.

508
30:19.489 --> 30:21.291
I'll do my best, Mr. Onizuka.

509
30:26.029 --> 30:26.963
Comeback.

510
30:28.331 --> 30:29.432
You have to…

511
30:30.199 --> 30:31.834
study super hard

512
30:33.036 --> 30:34.237
and become a big shot.

513
30:35.872 --> 30:38.541
And, along with everyone here…

514
30:39.409 --> 30:41.978
become a hero who saves many people.

515
30:43.546 --> 30:44.881
I wonder if I can do it?

516
30:44.948 --> 30:48.418
As long as you don't forget to stay close to others

517
30:49.085 --> 30:50.586
and keep cherishing your grandma,

518
30:51.754 --> 30:52.956
you'll be just fine.

519
30:56.125 --> 30:58.561
Understood, Mr. Onizuka.

520
31:05.168 --> 31:06.102
Hero.

521
31:07.804 --> 31:10.206
Don't forget about the time you injured your hand.

522
31:11.207 --> 31:12.308
Thanks to that,

523
31:13.042 --> 31:17.480
you were able to grow both as an athlete and as a person.

524
31:18.815 --> 31:19.949
That's true.

525
31:21.751 --> 31:24.187
When you make it to the Premier League,

526
31:24.988 --> 31:28.224
I can brag that you were my student. I'm looking forward to it.

527
31:32.095 --> 31:33.596
You have the courage

528
31:34.197 --> 31:37.900
to throw yourself in harm's way to protect everyone, so you can make it.

529
31:39.435 --> 31:41.571
Thank you, Mr. Onizuka.

530
31:48.111 --> 31:49.112
Seishin.

531
31:50.947 --> 31:52.382
When you decided

532
31:53.716 --> 31:57.053
this was the school you were meant to attend, I was so happy.

533
31:59.222 --> 32:01.724
You have limitless potential.

534
32:02.792 --> 32:03.960
So from now on,

535
32:06.062 --> 32:08.164
never think of others as fools,

536
32:08.731 --> 32:11.334
and don't think of yourself as one, either.

537
32:12.568 --> 32:13.403
Yeah.

538
32:14.170 --> 32:16.672
I won't do that anymore, Mr. Onizuka.

539
32:22.478 --> 32:23.446
MY.

540
32:24.947 --> 32:28.418
When you said you wanted to enjoy

541
32:29.352 --> 32:33.289
your youth with everyone, and took the nickname "Miss Youth"

542
32:33.356 --> 32:37.393
to symbolize it, I was so happy.

543
32:39.695 --> 32:42.899
You're way more mature than me,

544
32:43.666 --> 32:45.935
so trust yourself and have a wonderful romance.

545
32:47.637 --> 32:50.840
Do it for Ayumu too. He really liked you.

546
32:52.909 --> 32:55.178
I will, Mr. Onizuka.

547
32:58.881 --> 32:59.849
Secretary-General.

548
33:00.583 --> 33:05.688
You have to live up to your nickname and become a man who leads the world.

549
33:06.622 --> 33:09.092
Go straight toward your dreams.

550
33:09.592 --> 33:14.897
Even if you don't reach the finish line, pushing forward toward your dream

551
33:15.665 --> 33:18.401
is never wasted effort, so I'll be cheering for you.

552
33:19.735 --> 33:21.938
Thank you, Mr. Onizuka.

553
33:28.678 --> 33:29.779
TC.

554
33:31.647 --> 33:34.817
When I heard you say you wanted to work

555
33:35.451 --> 33:38.387
at the same school as Ms. Kashiwabara someday,

556
33:38.454 --> 33:41.357
I actually got goosebumps and tears in my eyes.

557
33:42.692 --> 33:44.393
When someone is in trouble,

558
33:44.927 --> 33:48.097
you look beautiful acting without hesitation.

559
33:48.998 --> 33:51.100
I look forward to the day you become

560
33:52.168 --> 33:53.402
Great Teacher Cocoa.

561
33:54.504 --> 33:57.273
When that time comes, come visit me, Mr. Onizuka.

562
34:04.013 --> 34:04.881
Mr. Onizuka,

563
34:05.448 --> 34:07.817
I'm sorry… it's all my fault.

564
34:10.786 --> 34:14.257
You were the only one who didn't have a nickname, Soma.

565
34:15.391 --> 34:16.459
What would you like?

566
34:19.462 --> 34:22.198
Call me "Chairperson."

567
34:24.734 --> 34:27.537
I want to become a person like my grandma.

568
34:31.140 --> 34:33.743
Everyone, Soma's grandma

569
34:34.510 --> 34:38.447
is the person I respect most out of everyone I've met in my life.

570
34:40.650 --> 34:41.751
Both of us

571
34:42.785 --> 34:45.154
must live in a way that wouldn't make her ashamed.

572
34:46.556 --> 34:47.657
Chairperson.

573
34:49.225 --> 34:51.260
Yes, Mr. Onizuka.

574
34:52.495 --> 34:54.063
To my beloved wife.

575
34:54.130 --> 34:55.565
Right now,

576
34:56.165 --> 34:59.268
for the first time, I feel like I've become a real teacher.

577
35:00.069 --> 35:05.174
Until now, I thought my job was to help the students grow.

578
35:06.475 --> 35:07.376
But in reality,

579
35:07.877 --> 35:11.914
these kids were helping me grow.

580
35:12.582 --> 35:15.184
I've finally realized it.

581
35:23.259 --> 35:26.429
With this, I've said all my goodbyes.

582
35:29.532 --> 35:31.734
Hey, you ruined the moment!

583
35:32.235 --> 35:38.040
My bad, I stayed up all night yesterday trying to think of cool things to say.

584
35:41.210 --> 35:42.578
Twenty-eight students,

585
35:43.546 --> 35:44.914
not a single one missing.

586
35:48.651 --> 35:49.952
It's a perfect number.

587
35:58.728 --> 35:59.795
See you.

588
36:16.479 --> 36:20.216
I forgot to tell you something.

589
36:22.852 --> 36:24.120
You are all

590
36:25.254 --> 36:26.389
great!

591
36:45.441 --> 36:46.909
This is good, huh, Principal?

592
37:01.123 --> 37:04.994
Ms. Kashiwabara, Class 1-B is pretty amazing, right?

593
37:05.061 --> 37:09.398
Still, I wish Mr. Onizuka could have seen this too.

594
37:09.465 --> 37:11.500
He's probably feeling lonely right now.

595
37:15.938 --> 37:18.841
Touch, touch, friends!

596
37:18.908 --> 37:21.677
Touch, touch, friends!

597
37:21.744 --> 37:24.613
Touch, touch, friends!

598
37:35.358 --> 37:38.094
DRILL TEAM

599
37:41.230 --> 37:44.266
We're going to transform!

600
37:55.711 --> 37:57.113
Mr. Onizuka!

601
38:01.217 --> 38:03.853
I finally understand.

602
38:05.287 --> 38:06.288
Understand what?

603
38:06.856 --> 38:11.827
The reason you got fired from every school you've ever been to.

604
38:12.395 --> 38:15.297
Just like this time, you tried to protect the students.

605
38:15.865 --> 38:16.899
Well…

606
38:17.466 --> 38:20.469
I mean, it's my job as a teacher, after all.

607
38:20.536 --> 38:24.073
But aren't you frustrated that you couldn't see them graduate?

608
38:28.978 --> 38:32.014
Of course I'm frustrated!

609
38:32.681 --> 38:33.716
How could I not be?

610
38:34.283 --> 38:35.351
Then why?

611
38:37.253 --> 38:38.621
Ms. Kashiwabara,

612
38:39.855 --> 38:42.291
this time, it's because you're here.

613
38:43.592 --> 38:44.593
What?

614
38:45.561 --> 38:46.629
The rest,

615
38:47.863 --> 38:49.031
I'll leave to you.

616
38:56.372 --> 38:57.673
I understand.

617
39:08.284 --> 39:09.485
Hey, why are you crying?

618
39:09.552 --> 39:11.554
Because I'm just so happy…

619
39:11.620 --> 39:13.456
Your dream came true, Yuukichi.

620
39:14.690 --> 39:15.624
Ken-Ken.

621
39:15.691 --> 39:16.625
What?

622
39:17.393 --> 39:18.961
Should we start dating?

623
39:19.695 --> 39:20.729
Seriously?

624
39:20.796 --> 39:22.364
One, two!

625
39:22.431 --> 39:26.235
Let's make it a good day!

626
39:37.746 --> 39:39.148
SEISHIN FESTIVAL

627
39:47.056 --> 39:49.959
Great!

628
39:52.361 --> 39:55.531
Teacher!

629
39:57.433 --> 40:00.236
Onicchi!

630
40:01.904 --> 40:06.041
In the end, I got fired again, huh?

631
40:06.108 --> 40:09.245
And the answer to what a "Great Teacher" really is…

632
40:10.079 --> 40:11.614
I never found it either.

633
40:26.395 --> 40:27.229
Welcome home.

634
40:27.997 --> 40:29.031
What?

635
40:29.098 --> 40:31.166
I'm making my favorite hamburger steaks today.

636
40:31.934 --> 40:33.669
What's with the shirt?

637
40:33.736 --> 40:35.704
What? Oh…

638
40:35.771 --> 40:37.006
Didn't I tell you?

639
40:37.573 --> 40:41.544
I went to relax in Hawaii, so I couldn't reply to your texts. Sorry.

640
40:42.344 --> 40:43.445
Right.

641
40:44.079 --> 40:45.214
I see.

642
40:46.382 --> 40:49.718
So, how are things at school?

643
40:51.554 --> 40:53.622
I'm sorry, I got fired.

644
40:54.890 --> 40:56.892
What? Again?

645
40:56.959 --> 41:00.429
Oh, no… Well, it's just like you said, Azusa,

646
41:01.030 --> 41:03.732
I'm really a useless man.

647
41:04.533 --> 41:06.035
Even with Soma,

648
41:06.101 --> 41:11.840
there might have been a better solution, but I couldn't think of anything at all.

649
41:11.907 --> 41:13.275
DIVORCE FORM

650
41:17.746 --> 41:18.781
Then…

651
41:19.782 --> 41:21.784
don't forget that feeling, okay?

652
41:28.223 --> 41:29.091
What do you mean?

653
41:29.725 --> 41:32.494
At the end of the day, you were never a teacher!

654
41:33.162 --> 41:35.798
You only think of students as friends,

655
41:35.864 --> 41:38.500
and you can only see things from their perspective.

656
41:40.669 --> 41:41.537
I'm sorry…

657
41:41.604 --> 41:44.573
What are you talking about? That's your good quality!

658
41:45.507 --> 41:48.711
You don't see things from an adult's perspective.

659
41:48.777 --> 41:50.879
You interact with students like a friend.

660
41:50.946 --> 41:53.782
Isn't a teacher like that a Great Teacher?

661
41:54.617 --> 41:57.820
Besides, even at your age, after all this time,

662
41:57.886 --> 42:00.422
you're still trying to become a genuine teacher.

663
42:00.956 --> 42:02.191
Isn't that amazing?

664
42:06.228 --> 42:07.262
Thank you.

665
42:10.099 --> 42:11.266
Also…

666
42:11.834 --> 42:12.901
Also?

667
42:13.469 --> 42:15.904
The hamburger steaks are burning.

668
42:19.008 --> 42:21.210
Oh no! I messed up!

669
42:23.178 --> 42:24.179
There.

670
42:25.948 --> 42:27.249
Keep it inside.

671
42:28.017 --> 42:30.753
Mr. Onizuka, how are you doing?

672
42:34.056 --> 42:36.825
Everyone in Class 1-B is doing well.

673
42:42.931 --> 42:43.966
Oh, right,

674
42:44.033 --> 42:47.636
the Principal started commuting by motorcycle.

675
42:48.303 --> 42:53.709
Turns out, just like you, Mr. Onizuka, he used to be a delinquent too.

676
42:53.776 --> 42:57.112
There are countless schools in this world.

677
42:57.179 --> 43:00.716
However, this Seishin High is different!

678
43:00.783 --> 43:05.154
I thought the Vice Principal would just quiet down and lay low,

679
43:06.689 --> 43:09.324
but he has helped deal with all the difficult parents,

680
43:09.391 --> 43:12.928
something we all hated to do. We're so grateful to him.

681
43:12.995 --> 43:14.496
Leave it to us.

682
43:14.997 --> 43:16.131
Hey.

683
43:16.732 --> 43:18.767
Aren't you supposed to be in supplementary class?

684
43:18.834 --> 43:21.370
All the other teachers are doing their best

685
43:22.171 --> 43:25.507
for the students too, in their own ways.

686
43:26.241 --> 43:27.509
You're great.

687
43:27.576 --> 43:31.146
Let's make today a good day too.

688
43:31.714 --> 43:35.551
For some reason, I feel like everyone is copying you, Mr. Onizuka.

689
43:36.585 --> 43:38.420
Good morning.

690
43:38.487 --> 43:40.522
Good morning.

691
43:40.589 --> 43:44.693
All right, all 28 of you are here today, not a single one missing, right?

692
43:45.494 --> 43:47.096
Yes!

693
43:47.162 --> 43:49.064
Okay, we're doing a pop quiz.

694
43:49.131 --> 43:50.365
What?

695
43:51.233 --> 43:52.768
No complaining.

696
43:52.835 --> 43:55.571
It'll be fine. Your grades have been going up, after all.

697
43:59.374 --> 44:01.643
Still, I can say this for sure.

698
44:02.678 --> 44:07.816
Seishin High is on its way to becoming a wonderful school.

699
44:10.519 --> 44:13.455
Why did you apply to our school?

700
44:15.357 --> 44:16.391
Is something wrong?

701
44:17.426 --> 44:18.961
Oh, I'm sorry.

702
44:19.862 --> 44:23.966
A long time ago, someone asked me a similar question,

703
44:24.700 --> 44:28.837
and I answered, "Because I wanted to become a teacher."

704
44:30.038 --> 44:31.240
Then, what about now?

705
44:32.407 --> 44:35.210
Well, now it's because…

706
44:39.381 --> 44:42.484
I want to become a real teacher.

707
44:46.188 --> 44:47.156
Subtitle translation by: Nix S.
